BY020 [*] `cast` call can be written as the `cast!` keyword
 --> BY020.by:5:9
  |
4 | def f(value: object) -> int:
5 |     n = cast(int, value)
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
6 |     print(cast(str, value))
7 |     _ = cast(int, value) + 1
  |
help: Replace with `cast!`
  |
4 | def f(value: object) -> int:
  -     n = cast(int, value)
5 +     n = value cast! int
6 |     print(cast(str, value))
  |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

BY020 [*] `cast` call can be written as the `cast!` keyword
